WEBVTT

00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:18,280
Last week, you said you weren't a fan of black pepper because it makes everything in your gut absorb better.

00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:26,780
Is this the same thing, is the same thing true of red hot peppers or hot red pepper flakes?

00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:38,780
No, no, so it was discovered years ago that black pepper helped you absorb different nutrients.

00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:44,780
So they actually started putting black pepper because it would take a step back.

00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:54,780
Many nutrients in the nutraceutical industry over the years have been discovered to be great for certain things.

00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:07,780
But the problem was the form of that nutrient that was available at the time, many times with many of the different nutrients was not really well absorbed.

00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:18,780
It was like glutathione as an example. Probably about 15 years ago, the form of glutathione that we used with patients, not with our cancer patients, forever.

00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:25,780
But what we used with fiber myelogen autoimmune patients and things was not readily absorbed.

00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:35,780
So we used to create, in our clinic, we used to make our own liposomal glutathione for the sake of absorbability.

00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:45,780
Are we used to have people nebulize glutathione, dissolve it in a liquid water and then nebulize it in order to increase the absorption?

00:01:45,780 --> 00:02:06,780
Well, then over time they started increasing the, you know, battery, the product itself with different testing and absorbability of different nutrients and glutathione in our example has gone through multiple different changes in the product, multiple endpoint product that is distributed and sold.

00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:11,780
And now glutathione, even in L, glutathione is much more absorbable.

00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:16,780
Now they also have liposomal glutathione things. So it's much more absorbable.

00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:22,780
But during this time, they found that black pepper helped things absorb.

00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:28,780
And one of the studies was done on curcumin and black pepper and it really increased absorbability.

00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:35,780
So a lot of companies added black pepper to their curcumin and I'm not against using black pepper in your curcumin.

00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:48,780
But if you're adding black pepper to a lot of different supplements that you're taking, you will increase the absorbability of other things that are in the gut, maybe things you don't want to absorb.

00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:50,780
So you have to be careful with that.

00:02:50,780 --> 00:03:01,780
So, but that is not true with hot pepper, cayenne pepper and red pepper flakes so you're safe with those.

